          "content": "Certainly! Below is a structured 12-section study guide for introductory probability. Each section includes key concepts, formulas, and practice problems to help you understand and apply the principles of probability.\n\n### Section 1: Introduction to Probability\n- **Definition of Probability**: The likelihood of an event occurring.\n- **Sample Space**: The set of all possible outcomes of an experiment.\n- **Event**: A subset of the sample space.\n- **Probability Scale**: Values range from 0 (impossible) to 1 (certain).\n\n**Practice Problem**: If you roll a fair six-sided die, what is the probability of rolling a 4?\n\n### Section 2: Basic Probability Rules\n- **Addition Rule**: \\( P(A \\cup B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A \\cap B) \\)\n- **Multiplication Rule**: \\( P(A \\cap B) = P(A) \\cdot P(B|A) \\)\n- **Complement Rule**: \\( P(A^c) = 1 - P(A) \\)\n\n**Practice Problem**: If the probability of rain on any given day in a city is 0.3, what is the probability that it will not rain on a particular day?\n\n### Section 3",
          "role": "assistant"
        }
      }
